\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces HJ-Biplot of TAM questionnaire responses ($n=25$). Dimension~1 explains 43.6\,\% of variance; Dimension~2 explains 24.2\,\% (cumulative: 67.8\,\%). Arrows indicate item vectors; proximity of participant points to a vector reflects agreement with that item. The UP cluster (PTAM001--006) and most FUP items (PTAM008--010) point in the same direction, indicating high internal correlation. PTAM007 and PTAM012 are orthogonal to the main cluster, capturing independent variance.}}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:biplot}{{3}{14}{}{figure.3}{}}
